16 · SEQUENTIAL IMPLEMENTATION AND CHANGE CONTROL

Work in-place and in controlled phases.

Do not rewrite the entire project in one uncontrolled pass.

Before each phase:

1. Read the latest verified project state.
2. Read the source files affected by the phase.
3. Identify existing active owners.
4. Compare against the approved design system.
5. Define exact intended changes.
6. Implement only the authorized scope.
7. Test the affected functionality.
8. Perform visual and regression verification.
9. Report actual outcomes.
10. Stop before the next phase.

Maintain a file-level change log.

Never present a speculative fix as tested.

Never delete an existing implementation merely because another version looks cleaner.

