17 · FOUR EXECUTION PHASES

PHASE 01: CORE ENGINE, FIBER AND ISOLATION

Establish the rendering and motion architecture.

Scope:

* Audit active React and Three.js code paths.
* Confirm React Three Fiber compatibility.
* Establish renderer lifecycle and scene ownership.
* Establish the authoritative camera rig.
* Integrate Theatre.js where compatible.
* Define motion scheduling and GSAP ownership.
* Establish material/shader registries.
* Isolate event handling and component state.
* Resolve verified runtime conflicts.
* Configure responsive rendering and quality presets.

Acceptance gate: One coherent renderer architecture, documented component ownership, functioning camera control and no known conflicting render or animation ownership.

Stop and report the exact files changed.

PHASE 02: 3D ASSETS, MATERIALS AND CINEMATIC MOTION

Implement the approved visual system.

Scope:

* Import and verify approved 3D assets.
* Apply correct material textures and PBR settings.
* Implement approved custom shaders.
* Configure cinematic lighting.
* Establish the postprocessing pipeline.
* Implement named Theatre.js sequences.
* Configure continuous camera paths.
* Create animation and camera registries.
* Validate visual fidelity against references.

Acceptance gate: Approved visual elements are implemented, controllable and visually verified at specified reference states.

Stop and report the exact changes and outstanding issues.

PHASE 03: DATA, INTERACTIONS AND VOICE

Connect real behavior to the cinematic environment.

Scope:

* Preserve existing data contracts.
* Build or reconcile approved information visualizations.
* Connect charts and spatial graphics to actual data.
* Implement component interaction APIs.
* Connect voice actions through defined controllers.
* Implement interruption and handoff behavior.
* Verify interactive states and lifecycle cleanup.
* Test motion ownership under simultaneous interactions.

Acceptance gate: Interactive components work without conflicting ownership, fabricated data or unauthorized voice changes.

Stop and report the evidence.

PHASE 04: EDITORIAL UI, SOCIAL CAPTURE AND FINAL QA

Implement the visual communication system and final integration.

Scope:

* Apply editorial typography and layout.
* Implement 75/25 visual-first composition.
* Complete infographic and motion-graphic treatments.
* Implement portrait and landscape compositions.
* Verify Arabic and RTL.
* Implement supported screenshot/capture modes.
* Test full WebGL and DOM compositing.
* Validate social safe areas.
* Test Safari and Chrome on available devices.
* Perform screenshot comparisons.
* Test motion and camera continuity.
* Measure performance.
* Run regression checks.
* Produce final component, asset and motion indexes.

Acceptance gate: Evidence-backed visual, functional, responsive and performance verification.

Do not call the project production-ready when required checks remain unverified.

